    not_duplicate_of: []  # ba4a
    pr_ref:  # ba4a
    description: "## Origin\n\nMaterialized 2026-06-04 from the 2026-06-03 fold-audit (Family J). Consolidates F34.A1 + F35.A1 previously folded onto INV-luhur. Full evidence remains across INV-luhur's pass-34 and pass-35 discussion entries; this row provides discrete representation.\n\nThe audit's verdict: STANDALONE because the INV-sugat closure's \"zero violations\" claim and WI-kafar's CI gate operate against a default substrate only — writer code paths gated behind `--frameworks all` and `--include-docs` escape the validator. Same root cause family across two analyzer cohorts.\n\n## Symptom\n\nTwo writer-code-path cohorts escape WI-kafar's CI gate:\n\n**F34.A1 — `--frameworks all` code paths (33 violations).** Pass-34 ran the validator against /tmp/p34_fw_all_bm.json (substrate generated with `--frameworks all`). 33 violations surface:\n- 20 axis_conformance (route-materializer 19 + grpc-linker 11 + graphql-linker 2 — but cross-codebase decomposition varies; root has 19+11+2, tracker has 20+0+0)\n- 13 id_format\n\nThese writers are gated behind `--frameworks all` and only fire when that flag is set. WI-kafar's default-substrate gate doesn't exercise them.\n\n**F35.A1 — `--include-docs` code paths (4321 violations, 130× larger).** Pass-35 ran the validator against /tmp/p35_docs_bm.json. 4321 id_format violations across 3 sub-mechanisms:\n- (a) gitignore writers REUSE Symbol.id as Symbol.stable_id — 2667 cases\n- (b) markdown section IDs include literal colons unsanitized — 825 cases\n- (c) markdown code_block emits 'code' literal as span segment — 584 cases\n\nSame root cause family: doc/config analyzer writers gated behind `--include-docs`.\n\n## Cross-codebase scope\n\n| Flag | ROOT violations | TRACKER violations |\n|---|---|---|\n| `--frameworks all` | 33 | 20 |\n| `--include-docs` | 4321 | 102 (markdown only) |\n\nPattern verified across codebases — the validator escape is structural, not codebase-specific.\n\n## Invariant\n\nWI-kafar's CI validator gate exercises EVERY writer code path, including those gated behind `--frameworks all`, `--include-docs`, `--no-handler-slices`, and any other flag-gated writers. Either:\n\n1. **Multi-substrate test matrix.** Validator runs against default + each flag-mode substrate, asserts zero violations on all.\n2. **Flag-conditional emission moved to default path.** Doc analyzers and framework linkers fire by default; the violations get fixed at the producer level so flag-gating is unnecessary.\n\nPath (1) is cheaper but adds N substrate generations to CI. Path (2) is the structural fix but requires the producer fixes to land first.\n\n## Fix sketch\n\nPhase 1: Add `--frameworks all` and `--include-docs` substrates to WI-kafar's CI matrix; assert zero violations on both. Surfaces remaining producer-side bugs.\n\nPhase 2 (followups): each violation cohort gets its own fix-PR. The pass-35 sub-mechanism breakdown (gitignore / markdown-section-id / markdown-code_block) cleanly partitions into 3 PRs.\n\n## Source provenance\n\n- **F34.A1** — INV-luhur discussion entry 2026-06-02 (pass-34 batch; FIRST validator-scope blind spot at 33 violations on --fw all).\n- **F35.A1** — INV-luhur + INV-kurup discussion entries 2026-06-02 (pass-35 batch; SECOND validator-scope blind spot at 4321 violations on --include-docs).\n- F40.D1 supporting — pass-40 confirmed both F34.A1=33 and F35.A1=4321 EXACT-MATCH; methodology robust.\n\nLab notebooks: passes 34, 35, 40 under `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/`.\n\n## Related rows\n\n- Parent: **INV-luhur** (writer-contract META).\n- Sibling: **WI-kafar** (existing CI gate — this row extends its scope).\n- Sibling: **INV-kurup** (existing identifier-format META; F35.A1's 3 sub-mechanisms all under INV-kurup scope).\n- Sibling: **WI-bazij-validator-denominator-doc** (Family J — adjacent validator gap).\n- Sibling: **INV-sugat** (satisfied META; this row reopens its \"zero violations\" claim under non-default substrates)."  # ba4a
    fields: {}  # ba4a
